  "basis": "The chart's color legend explicitly maps color to incidence values: light yellow corresponds to 'High' (100) and dark red to 'Low' (0). Among the three options, New Hampshire (NH) is colored very pale yellow, Delaware (DE) is orange, and Florida (FL) is dark burgundy. Therefore, NH has the highest incidence value, DE is intermediate, and FL has the lowest among the three. The task requires routing to the state with the highest prevalence (incidence), which is NH.",
